<Base title="Methodology"><div class="shell page-intro"><div class="section-label">HOW WE TRACK / METHODOLOGY</div><h1>Evidence before<br /><em>assumption.</em></h1><p>TrackYourInfra is designed as a public record. A useful update needs a source, a date and enough context for someone else to check it.</p></div><div class="shell methodology-layout"><nav class="method-nav" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#demonstration-data">Demonstration data</a><a href="#status">Project status</a><a href="#confidence">Confidence</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a><a href="#contribute">Contribution roadmap</a></nav><div class="method-content"><section id="demonstration-data"><div class="section-label">01 / CURRENT DATA</div><h2>Phase 1 uses invented records.</h2><p>The three corridors, routes, milestone dates, cost figures and progress values are demonstration content. They exist to test navigation and visual design. They are not statements about real infrastructure projects, and the map lines are not surveyed alignments.</p><p>Before launch, these records should be replaced by verified projects with primary sources and reviewed geography.</p></section><section id="status"><div class="section-label">02 / LIFECYCLE</div><h2>Status describes a stage.</h2><div class="definition-grid"><div><strong>Proposed</strong><p>Publicly discussed; formal approval not established.</p></div><div><strong>Approved</strong><p>Relevant authority has formally approved it.</p></div><div><strong>Funded</strong><p>Funding has been confirmed.</p></div><div><strong>Tendering</strong><p>Procurement is underway.</p></div><div><strong>Under construction</strong><p>Physical work has started.</p></div><div><strong>Partially operational</strong><p>Some sections are open.</p></div><div><strong>Operational</strong><p>The tracked scope is open.</p></div><div><strong>Delayed / cancelled</strong><p>A dated source confirms the change.</p></div></div></section><section id="confidence"><div class="section-label">03 / CONFIDENCE</div><h2>Confidence is about evidence.</h2><p><strong>High</strong> means supported by primary documents or multiple corroborating sources. <strong>Medium</strong> means credible reporting or verified observations. <strong>Low</strong> means an early or illustrative report requiring further review. Every Phase 1 demonstration record is marked low.</p></section><section id="sources"><div class="section-label">04 / PROVENANCE</div><h2>Keep the trail visible.</h2><p>For each important claim, the site records its source, publication date, status date and last update. Unknown values stay blank rather than being inferred. Later revisions should remain visible through the public repository history.</p></section><section id="contribute"><div class="section-label">05 / WHAT'S NEXT</div><h2>Community review comes next.</h2><p>Phase 2 will define structured reports, source submission, pull request review and maintainers for each geography. The website and data will live in one open MIT licensed repository.</p><a class="button button-primary" href="/projects">Explore the prototype <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section></div></div></Base>
